.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1015 AM PDT Sat Oct 3 2026

High pressure strengthening over the region will result in
continued VFR conditions throughout the day today with weak
onshore flow returning by mid-afternoon before easing overnight.
The greatest potential for sub-IFR conditions will be around the
Monterey Bay terminals late tonight into early Sunday morning,
however confidence is low to moderate.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Weak offshore winds currently with weak
onshore flow expected by mid-afternoon. Winds ease overnight and
into early Sunday morning with generally high confidence of VFR
conditions persisting through the TAF period.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Moderate drainage winds currently
at SNS will shift onshore by early afternoon and prevail through
this evening. The greatest potential for sub-IFR conditions will
be at MRY late tonight and into early Sunday morning, less
confidence for SNS. Any low clouds and/or fog that does develop is
likely to dissipate by 15Z Sunday.

