.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 458 AM PDT Sat Oct 3 2026

Hot and dry conditions are forecast through next week, which will
be accompanied with weak offshore flow. Poor to very poor
overnight recovery is expected for the thermal belts, generally
for elevations above 1000-1500 feet, leading to elevated fire
weather conditions. The marine layer is expected to be confined to
the immediate coast and around 500 feet. A pattern change begins
late Thursday into Friday, which may lead to cooler weather and
the potential for improved RH recovery.

